<title>CHINA: China's Daqing field pumps 56 mln T of oil in 1996.</title>
<headline>China's Daqing field pumps 56 mln T of oil in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>BEIJING 1997-01-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>China's Daqing oilfield, the nation's largest, pumped a record 56 million tonnes of crude oil in 1996, the China News Service said on Monday.</p>
<p>Production at the field in China's northeastern Heilongjiang province had remained steady since passing an annual 50 million tonnes in 1976, the agency said.</p>
<p>Tests showed the field would continue to be able to produce around 50 million tonnes a year until 2010, it said but gave no further details. -- Beijing newsroom (8610) 65321921</p>
</text>
